{
  "locale": "zh-Hans",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "系统更换组成部分后，“持续”指的不是每个组成部分都保持原样，而是系统能够不断重新组织和协调这些部分，维持自身的运行方式。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "因此，持续是一种动态能力：部分结构改变时，其余结构能够重新调整；原有路径失效时，新的路径能够建立；环境变化时，组织方式能够适应。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "与此相比，“原样不变”可理解为保持既有组成或状态不发生改变；现有片段说明，持续并不是这种静态结果，而是变化之中的连续组织能力。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "不过，系统仍能继续运行并不必然意味着它能够持续地更新自己；如果继续依赖不断增加的投入或补偿，并持续消耗恢复空间，就可能只是维持表面的连续，而不是保留下一轮继续所需的条件。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-ebb6043df46c213571580cbf64914e0bdced10965da83aa75968d3befde5a41a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "更换组成部分本身也会产生维护需求，因为每次运行都会改变下一次运行的起点，并可能增加新的依赖、接口、流程或责任关系。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-8c1bdea46e93d08811f233ab30dcdea5eeab42aafe67879696bbf1c207d6592a"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sourceLanguages": [
    "zh-Hans"
  ],
  "status": "answered_with_scope_limit",
  "boundary": "片段支持“持续”与静态保持原样之间的区别，也支持组成部分发生改变时通过重新组织维持运行；但未对“原样不变”给出独立的正式定义，因此这里将其限定为对既有组成或状态的静态保持，而非更广泛的概念。"
}

{
  "locale": "zh-Hans",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "整体的持续不依赖每一个固定部件不变，而依赖系统不断重新组织部件，并持续维持自身的运行方式。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "当部件发生更新或变化时，整体需要能够重新调整其余结构；当原有路径失效时，需要逐渐建立新的路径；面对环境变化时，组织方式需要持续适应。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "整体还需要能够不断恢复自身、面对扰动，并保持连续运行；因此，稳定并不意味着没有变化，而意味着在变化中仍具备持续组织自身的能力。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "要使持续不只是把当前状态延长到未来，当前运行还需要保留下一轮继续所需的条件：资源使用与负荷释放之间需要保持关系，已经结束的责任需要能够退出，结构需要能够修正，经验需要能够进入下一轮。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-ebb6043df46c213571580cbf64914e0bdced10965da83aa75968d3befde5a41a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "由于每一轮运行都会改变下一轮运行的起点，整体还需要处理运行产生的历史、依赖、责任和维护要求；否则表面的连续可能只是依靠持续增加投入来维持，并会削弱未来继续的条件。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-8c1bdea46e93d08811f233ab30dcdea5eeab42aafe67879696bbf1c207d6592a",
        "F-ebb6043df46c213571580cbf64914e0bdced10965da83aa75968d3befde5a41a"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sourceLanguages": [
    "zh-Hans"
  ],
  "status": "supported",
  "boundary": "上述证据支持的是整体持续所需的组织、恢复、适应、资源与维护条件；未明确给出一套穷尽性的条件清单，也未证明每项条件单独构成整体持续的充分条件。"
}

{
  "locale": "zh-Hans",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "正常维持发生得更早，针对的是系统仍能运行但其承载条件正在逐渐改变的状态；它重点处理持续运行所产生的后果，而不是等到结构明显损坏后再修理。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-0b99d2d8edfe06d9c771891ea3d36420a8ee77a5456a9b98fda2407489166a9f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "发生损坏或扰动后的恢复，则是在既有结构、路径或运行方式受到影响后，重新组织和调整系统，使整体运行得以恢复或继续；这不要求原有组成部分完全不变。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-0b99d2d8edfe06d9c771891ea3d36420a8ee77a5456a9b98fda2407489166a9f",
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "因此，两者的主要区别在于时点和任务：维持是在尚能运行时保护继续运行所需的条件，恢复是在出现明显损坏或扰动后，通过修理、重新调整或建立替代路径来恢复整体运行。所给片段没有进一步说明具体修复步骤、判断阈值或资源要求。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-0b99d2d8edfe06d9c771891ea3d36420a8ee77a5456a9b98fda2407489166a9f",
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sourceLanguages": [
    "zh-Hans"
  ],
  "status": "supported_with_scope",
  "boundary": "以上比较仅限于所给片段：片段支持维护与明显损坏后的修理在时点和关注重点上的区别，也支持扰动后的重新组织与运行恢复；但未给出恢复流程、损坏等级、成功标准或具体操作方法。"
}

{
  "locale": "zh-Hans",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "不是。就这些片段所述，组织延续并不依靠冻结原有部件，而依靠不断重新组织内部元素、恢复整体运行并维持自身运行方式的能力。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "片段明确指出，某些结构发生改变时，其余结构可以重新调整；某些路径失效时，可以逐渐建立新的路径；因此，持续存在的重点不是固定元素本身，而是组织持续协调自身的能力。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "城市的例子也表明，建筑、道路、设施、人口和产业都可以更替，只要交通、资源、生产、交流与秩序等整体运行能够持续恢复，城市仍可保持连续运行。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "不过，部件更替并不意味着无需维护：每次运行都会改变下一次运行的起点，并可能留下新的经验、流程、资料、责任关系、依赖和兼容问题，因此持续运行需要处理这些后果。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-8c1bdea46e93d08811f233ab30dcdea5eeab42aafe67879696bbf1c207d6592a"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sourceLanguages": [
    "zh-Hans"
  ],
  "status": "answered",
  "boundary": "这些片段支持的是组织或系统在内部结构变化中的连续运行原则；未提供适用于所有组织的具体替换流程、部件保留比例或冻结期限。"
}

{
  "locale": "zh-Hans",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "维护与修理的差别在于时机和关注对象：修理通常发生在某个结构已经明显损坏之后；维护则更早，针对仍能运行的现实，关注其承载条件是否正在逐渐改变，并处理持续过程所产生的后果。",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-0b99d2d8edfe06d9c771891ea3d36420a8ee77a5456a9b98fda2407489166a9f"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sourceLanguages": [
    "zh-Hans"
  ],
  "status": "supported",
  "boundary": "该片段支持上述时机与关注对象的区别，但未进一步说明具体维护措施、修理措施或二者的适用范围；“仍能运行”也不等同于完全没有任何故障。"
}

{
  "locale": "en",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "An organization can endure because its continuity depends not on preserving every individual component, but on continually reorganizing those components and maintaining its way of operating.",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This endurance is a dynamic capacity: the organization must continually restore itself, respond to disturbances, adjust remaining structures when some change, establish new paths when old ones fail, and adapt its organization as conditions change.",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Thus, stability is not the absence of change; it is the continued coordination of change so that overall operation is preserved. The fragment illustrates this with a city whose buildings, roads, facilities, population, and industries change while transportation, resources, production, communication, and order continue.",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sourceLanguages": [
    "zh-Hans"
  ],
  "status": "answered",
  "boundary": "The fragment supports this account of continuity through reorganization, recovery, adaptation, and coordination. It does not specify how much replacement an organization can withstand, the exact conditions required for recovery, or whether every kind of organization behaves this way."
}

{
  "locale": "en",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "An organization can endure despite replacement of its constituent elements when it continually reorganizes those elements and maintains its mode of operation, rather than depending on every individual element remaining unchanged.",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This endurance is presented as a dynamic capacity: when parts change, remaining structures can readjust; when prior pathways cease to work, new pathways can gradually be established; and organizational arrangements can adapt to environmental change.",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The fragment illustrates this with a city: buildings, roads, facilities, population, and industries may change, while the city continues through its ability to restore overall functions such as transport, resources, production, exchange, and order.",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-1d3a288563890410a103383b6f1c33d31e56465a2ce7390c59105b4bee413edc"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sourceLanguages": [
    "zh-Hans"
  ],
  "status": "supported",
  "boundary": "The supplied fragment supports a general account of continuity through ongoing reorganization and adaptation, illustrated by a city. It does not specify necessary institutional mechanisms, thresholds of replacement, or criteria for determining when an organization has ceased to be the same organization."
}

{
  "locale": "en",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Repair usually occurs after a structure has already suffered obvious damage. Maintenance occurs earlier, while the structure is still able to operate, and concerns whether its load-bearing conditions are gradually changing. The fragment therefore supports a distinction between repair after evident damage and earlier maintenance of an still-functioning structure; it does not establish that maintenance always occurs before any damage at all.",
      "supportFragmentIds": [
        "F-0b99d2d8edfe06d9c771891ea3d36420a8ee77a5456a9b98fda2407489166a9f"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sourceLanguages": [
    "zh-Hans"
  ],
  "status": "supported_with_scope_limit",
  "boundary": "The supplied fragment supports the timing and operating-state distinction above, but provides no further criteria for what actions maintenance or repair involve."
}
